&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Every day, tens of millions of people come to Roblox to explore, create, play, learn, and connect with friends in 3D immersive digital experiences– all created by our global community of developers and creators.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Roblox, we’re building the tools and platform that empower our community to bring any experience that they can imagine to life. Our vision is to reimagine the way people come together, from anywhere in the world, and on any device.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re on a mission to connect a billion people with optimism and civility, and looking for amazing talent to help us get there.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A career at Roblox means you’ll be working to shape the future of human interaction, solving unique technical challenges at scale, and helping to create safer, more civil shared experiences for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roblox is seeking a Content Designer to join our Monetization team and drive the future of our platform&#39;s economy. In this role, you will play a crucial role in defining the content strategy and information architecture of strategic initiatives across Monetization, creating seamless and compelling experiences that empower both our users and creators. You will be a key player in shaping how we grow revenue, enhance developer earnings, and evolve our core monetization offerings within the Roblox ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and deliver UX content for key monetization surfaces and flows at Roblox, from early exploration through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of user and developer needs, behaviors, and motivations to inform content design decisions across payment, purchase, and monetization experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a fresh perspective and deep industry knowledge to drive innovation in monetization design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers, designers, researchers, and engineers to ensure experiences are valuable, understandable, and easy to use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply UX writing and content strategy to improve clarity, usability, and engagement across player, parent, and creator experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to building and maintaining content guidelines, patterns, and frameworks that support consistency in voice and tone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate and document content decisions clearly, using empathy, logic, research insights, and data to inform recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for high-quality content design within your area of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help improve team processes and collaboration by contributing to shared ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement AI solutions to improve content quality and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience in Product Design, User Experience Design, Graphic Design, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience (5+ years) in content design, with a strong portfolio demonstrating expertise in designing for e-commerce, payments, or innovative consumer experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking and a track record of designing comprehensive and connected user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of user-centered design principles, information architecture, e-commerce best practices, and monetization strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with and influencing cross-functional partners, including product managers, designers, researchers, and engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong drive to deeply understand product goals from both a business and user perspective, fostering a culture of learning and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to articulate content design concepts and rationale clearly and persuasively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset with the ability to work effectively across teams and influence design direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in the gaming industry, user-generated content platforms, and the creator economy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keen interest in user experience trends, fintech, and emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-motivated approach to continuously expand design skills and explore new tools and techniques, including a proven ability to incorporate AI into your workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For roles that are based at our headquarters in San Mateo, CA: The starting base pay for this position is as shown below. The actual base pay is dependent upon a variety of job-related factors such as professional background, training, work experience, location, business needs and market demand. Therefore, in some circumstances, the actual salary could fall outside of this expected range. This pay range is subject to change and may be modified in the future. All full-time employees are also eligible for equity compensation and for benefits as described on &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.roblox.com/total-rewards&quot;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$159,250&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$193,240 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Roles that are based in an office are onsite Tuesday, Wednesday, and Thursday, with optional presence on Monday and Friday (unless otherwise noted).&lt;/p&gt;
